      {
        "id": 115458,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-20T17:21:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Revo Corp is building in importance right now. &nbsp;We've had a few mentions, then images cleverly placed, then the mini-nemesis. &nbsp;I think more is coming. &nbsp;I think Revo Corp is the focal point of a much begger operation than the Organization, with possibly cosmic connections.</p><p>My thoughts on Revo Corp.</p><p>1. &nbsp;Revenant is a name heavily associated with returning from the dead. &nbsp;I think they are heavy into collecting defeated things. &nbsp;I think Chairman and Voss will be connected to Revo Corp, just like Omnitron was. &nbsp;They seem to be big into reverse engineering.</p><p>2. &nbsp;When did Revenant first show up in the timeline, and how does it relate timewise to Pike's disappearance? &nbsp;I'm wondering if Revenant is an alter ego of Pike, or someone who was in the shadows operating and now is coming out of said shadows. &nbsp;Pike was the Chairman of the Organization, but that implies others were involved. &nbsp;I can't help but think The Chairman or his assets are very important to Revo Corp.</p><p>3. &nbsp;I think that Revenant is Setback's nemesis because Setback is a successfully augmented human and Revo Corp wants to reverse engineer him to make more. &nbsp;They wanted the secret of Omnitron, and I think they have Voss as well, either as prisoner, subject or an important leader (depending on how Earth-centric they are). &nbsp;The Lazarus Chambers would be of incredible value to them, esp. if they could reverse-engineer Blade's work. &nbsp;Revo-Corp could very well be involved in Gloomweaver finding a host and Spite being reborn.</p><p>4. &nbsp;It would not surprise me at all if Ra's Staff was in Revo-Corp with the other relics, and I would love the new Ra to be someone from Revo-Corp, even if he was a bookkeeper or Janitor and not at all dedicated to some evil scheme. &nbsp;It would explain his reaction to Legacy.</p>",
