      {
        "id": 115465,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-20T19:08:03.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Oh I don't think the whole Revo-Corp thing is going down in the card game. &nbsp;It is still being set up in tactics. &nbsp;Voss could be back in the card game&nbsp;(I expect a promo for him),&nbsp;I don't know how well he fits Tactics, it would be very interesting though.&nbsp;I've been working on some of the villains converting them to Tactics, I might try to make a series of retro-scenarios if some good templates show up. &nbsp;Voss's Invasion is just too good a scenario to not use it. &nbsp;(have Spite half-done, but the \"play as a soul-less murderer\" scenario isn't sitting well in testing so I may bail on it)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Voss would work great in tactics. He could have an army of minions just like barons or omnitrons and be awesome.</p>\n<p>I think RevoCorp and FILTER still have a large role to play in the card game, and the final few expansions will likely flesh out their role further. But we know both organizations are still around during Tactics.</p>",
