      {
        "id": 115466,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-20T19:28:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>phantaskippy wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Oh I don't think the whole Revo-Corp thing is going down in the card game. &nbsp;It is still being set up in tactics. &nbsp;Voss could be back in the card game&nbsp;(I expect a promo for him),&nbsp;I don't know how well he fits Tactics, it would be very interesting though.&nbsp;I've been working on some of the villains converting them to Tactics, I might try to make a series of retro-scenarios if some good templates show up. &nbsp;Voss's Invasion is just too good a scenario to not use it. &nbsp;(have Spite half-done, but the \"play as a soul-less murderer\" scenario isn't sitting well in testing so I may bail on it)\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nVoss would work great in tactics. He could have an army of minions just like barons or omnitrons and be awesome.I think RevoCorp and FILTER still have a large role to play in the card game, and the final few expansions will likely flesh out their role further. But we know both organizations are still around during Tactics.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>But that is old Voss, and that would rock. &nbsp;New Voss isn't going to be running around like old Voss. &nbsp;Unless they really want to go Napoleon with him and have him escape, retake his home and set out to wipe out Earth. &nbsp;It is feasible, but I don't see them going back to the old Voss like that.</p>",
